Usage: ruralz bundle render [DIR] [FLAGS]

Render one Environment's one-file Bundle.

Writes the rendered Bundle of one Environment, a one-file Bundle in canonical
order with the overlay merged and ${VAR} substituted, as YAML or with --output
json as one JSON array. --effective prints the effective Filter Chains of every
Route, or with --route of one; --api-version VERSION --output-dir DIR converts
the source files to VERSION and checks that every Environment of
--environments keeps its Revision.

Arguments:
  DIR  Bundle directory, one-file Bundle, or - for standard input (default .)

Flags:
  --api-version VERSION    Convert the source files to VERSION, such as ruralz/v1alpha1 (needs --output-dir and --environments)
  --effective              Print the effective Filter Chains of every Route, or of --route
  --env NAME               Render with this Environment's overlay and variables, read from --environments
  --environments FILE      Local Environment resources
  --help                   Print this help
  --output yaml|json|text  Output format (yaml or json, default yaml; with --effective or --api-version: text or json, default text)
  --output-dir DIR         Directory of the converted files (needs --api-version)
  --output-file PATH       Write the data to PATH instead of standard output
  --route NAME             The Route of --effective
